[=DESCRIPTION]
Downloads CrowdStrike Falcon application inventory, Spotlight vulnerabilities, and
Configuration Assessment results, fetching all three datasets concurrently, and
writes them to a single JSON file or to per-dataset JSONL/XML files for downstream
ingestion. Supports host-group/tag scoping, FQL filtering, large-environment
parallelism, IAVM decoration, and per-AID output bucketing.
.PP
Credentials are read from a .env file (\fB\-\-env\-file\fR) or the environment. See
\fBFILES\fR and \fBENVIRONMENT\fR below.
.PP

[>ENVIRONMENT]
.TP
.B CLIENT_ID, CLIENT_SECRET
CrowdStrike API client credentials. Read from the environment when not supplied via
the \fB\-\-env\-file\fR. Environment variables take precedence over file values.
.TP
.B BASE_URL
Falcon API region/cloud (e.g. US1, US2, EU1, US-GOV-1). Default: US1.

[>FILES]
.TP
.B .env
Credentials file (CLIENT_ID, CLIENT_SECRET, BASE_URL). Read from the path given to
\fB\-\-env\-file\fR, or ./.env in the current directory. Holds API credentials; keep
it mode 0600.
.TP
.B <output-dir>/
Destination for multi-file output formats (jsonl, xml), including the manifest and
optional per-AID subdirectories.

[>EXAMPLES]
.TP
Fetch all datasets using a credentials file:
.B femur \-\-env\-file talon1.env
.TP
Write compact JSON to a specific file:
.B femur \-e talon1.env \-o results.json \-\-indent 0
.TP
Scope every dataset to host groups and filter vulnerabilities:
.B femur \-e talon1.env \-\-host\-groups "Production Servers" \-\-vuln\-filter "cve.severity:'CRITICAL'"
.TP
Large environment: enable the best-practice recipe and stream JSONL:
.B femur \-e talon1.env \-\-large\-env \-\-output\-dir ./inventory
.TP
Bucket output per agent ID and compress:
.B femur \-e talon1.env \-\-output\-dir ./inventory \-\-bucket\-by\-aid \-\-compress

[>SUPPORT]
FEMUR (Falcon Exposure Management Universal Reporter) is a community-driven, open
source project, not a CrowdStrike product. As such, it carries no formal support,
expressed or implied. For issue reporting guidance, questions, and confidentiality
considerations, see the project on GitHub:
.PP
.B https://github.com/cs-shadowbq/falcon-exposure-management-universal-reporter
.PP
Report issues at:
.B https://github.com/cs-shadowbq/falcon-exposure-management-universal-reporter/issues

[>SEE ALSO]
.B femurd (1)
serves the datasets produced by femur over HTTP.
.PP
Project documentation and installation guidance are distributed with the release:
INSTALL.md and the docs/ directory.
